(footprint "RotaryEncoder_HUANO_4.5mm_LayFlat_SMD"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "HUANO 4.5 mm mouse-wheel encoder (sold as MECCANIXITY, Amazon B0C13ZZVT5) laid on its back with the 1.74 mm hex bore up, pins pointing north and bent down onto top-side pads; the MP pads take the frame's two clip legs, bent down the same way. Origin = bore centre. Measured from a real part (HUANO publishes no drawing): body 9.54 wide x 8.34 long x 4.15 thick, bore 4.5 mm from the pin edge and 3.84 mm from the domed end, pins 3 mm long, 0.85 mm wide, 2.5 mm pitch. The pads run from 0.2 mm outside the body to the pin tips. Clip-leg positions estimated. Lay it on its black back with the marked metal face up: seen from that face with the pins down, the common pin is on the left (as on TT's and HOAUC's mouse-wheel encoders), so with the pins north it lands on the east pad (C). Hand-fitted, so no paste.")
	(tags "encoder wheel mouse HUANO 4.5 hex bore lay flat")
